# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-15); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: a laptop at a desk, with a big display to its right. The editor and the browser are docked on the big display and a
# chat floats between them, where its person put it. The lid closes: the laptop's display goes, the big one gets the menu bar,
# and every window has new coordinates without one of them saying so. Arbor hears a moment later, as on a Mac. Nothing moves on the
# glass, not then and not when the editor is next framed: the chat floats, and no view takes it away (Q29, 4). Then the lid
# opens again, and all is as it was. Where floating windows make way the chat leaves the view, and comes back to where it was
# on the glass: the second half.
# Spec: docs/features/F08-displays-and-spaces.md. Window ids start at 101.
quiet
plug desk right 2560x1440
open Code
open Safari
open Chat 400x500
move 101 1600 100 800 600
move 102 1700 150 800 600
cursor 2000 500
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
move 103 2500 400 400 500
wait 60
loud
expect docked 101
expect docked 102
expect floating 103
expect at 103 2500 400
# The lid closes. macOS has one display now, whose corner is 0,0; Arbor still believes in two.
quietly unplug main
expect at 103 1060 400
# A second and a half later it is told.
wait 2
report-displays
expect still
expect docked 101
expect docked 102
expect left-of 101 102
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect floating 103
expect at 103 1060 400
expect size 103 400x500
# The editor is framed, and then everything is shown again: the chat has stayed where it was on the glass.
zoom 101
expect hidden 102
expect still 103
expect visible 103
expect at 103 1060 400 400x500
home
expect still 103
expect at 103 1060 400
expect size 103 400x500
# The lid opens: the laptop is back on the left and has the menu bar again.
quietly plug main left 1440x900
quietly make-main main
expect at 103 2500 400
wait 2
report-displays
expect still
expect docked 101
expect docked 102
expect left-of 101 102
expect at 103 2500 400
cursor 2000 500
zoom 101
expect hidden 102
expect still 103
expect visible 103
expect at 103 2500 400 400x500
home
expect still 103
expect at 103 2500 400
expect size 103 400x500
# Only floating windows that make way leave with the Desktop. The same evening with those: wherever the chat is put back to, it is
# where it was on the glass, though the numbers have changed since Arbor last saw it there.
set floatingWindowsMakeWay true
expect still 103
wait 60
quietly unplug main
expect at 103 1060 400
wait 2
report-displays
expect still
expect at 103 1060 400
zoom 101
expect hidden 103
home
expect at 103 1060 400
expect size 103 400x500
quietly plug main left 1440x900
quietly make-main main
expect at 103 2500 400
wait 2
report-displays
expect still
expect at 103 2500 400
cursor 2000 500
zoom 101
expect hidden 103
home
expect at 103 2500 400
expect size 103 400x500
